#   file | reason | the matched word
#
# A reference to the OWNER is never declarable and never becomes declarable.
# Rewrite it: say the ROLE for a governance fact, and for anything else say what
# was wrong and what it measured.
#
# Checked BOTH WAYS — a declaration matching nothing any more is a failure, so a
# scrub cannot quietly un-cover a file by leaving a stale line here.
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS SOMEBODY ELSE'S TEXT, and none of it was typed in this
# repo. `data/` is the INGESTED corpus — OpenStreetMap and Wikidata descriptions
# of historical markers, artworks and place names, fetched by the workflows in
# `.github/workflows/` and committed as-is. The pronouns in it belong to the
# people those markers commemorate. Rewording them would be falsifying a source,
# which is the one thing an ingest must never do, so they are declared instead.
# `src/vendor/` is a third-party library whose comments cite its own author.
#
# THE RISK THIS ACCEPTS, written down because a declared exception is only safe
# while somebody knows what it covers: these entries are per FILE, and a
# re-ingest can put new text into the same file. That is tolerable because
# nothing about the owner is ever ingested — no workflow here writes anything
# but a fetch of a public source — and a hand-written note added to one of these
# files would be a change nobody intends.
